{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778942340,"nonce":"00VpY23nnWl1V9X+ftVIgWNeqB8=","message":"## Implementation design v0: ledger-backed graph projection\n\nThis issue should migrate the operational graph to ledger-derived structure without making the graph itself canonical storage.\n\n### Current state to preserve/replace\n\nCurrent graph routes build operational nodes from `IssueScanner`, `sessions`, `auth_requests`, `session_issues`, and `work_units`. Issue edges currently come from labels/body-derived data such as `parent:\u003cid\u003e`, and auth/session issue edges are inferred from JSON fields or commit messages.\n\nThe target is:\n\n- issue graph structure from `ledger_issues` and canonical relationship/link tables;\n- operational overlays from work units, auth requests, sessions, commits, and provider/artifact graph indices;\n- graph API payloads rich enough for deterministic layout and detail panes;\n- no git-bug subprocesses on graph request hot paths.\n\n### Backend module boundary\n\nAdd a projection module, probably `src/ledger/graph-adapter.ts`, consumed by `src/routes/graph.ts`.\n\nThe adapter should expose functions like:\n\n- `buildLedgerIssueGraph(params)`\n- `buildLedgerWorkGraph(params)`\n- `buildLedgerActivityGraph(params)`\n- `buildLedgerGraphFilters()`\n- `buildLedgerGraphModeCounts()`\n\nProvider/artifact modes can continue using `provider-artifacts.ts` initially. Do not regress provider-lineage/artifact-lineage/provenance modes.\n\n### Payload contract additions\n\nKeep `GraphPayload` backward compatible, but add optional fields rather than requiring a new frontend rewrite all at once.\n\nRecommended optional additions:\n\n```ts\ntype GraphNodeLayout = {\n  group_id?: string\n  role?: 'parent' | 'child' | 'annotation' | 'actor' | 'standalone'\n  rank?: number\n  order?: number\n  anchor_id?: string\n  collapsed_count?: number\n}\n\ntype GraphNodeAnnotation = {\n  id: string\n  type: 'auth_request' | 'session' | 'conflict' | 'sync' | 'work_unit'\n  label: string\n  status?: string\n  target?: string\n  count?: number\n}\n\ntype GraphNodeDetail = {\n  ledger_issue_id?: string\n  aliases?: string[]\n  project_id?: string\n  relationships?: Record\u003cstring, number\u003e\n  sync_state?: string\n  conflict_count?: number\n}\n```\n\nThese can live under existing `node.detail`, `node.summary`, and `node.visual` fields at first if changing shared types too much would cascade. The important point is to stop encoding layout semantics only through node type and force layout.\n\nFor edges, keep `metadata.label` and add `metadata.label_default_visible = false` for noisy labels. Edge labels should be off by default.\n\n### Issue mode\n\nIssue mode should mostly show issue nodes and semantic issue relationships.\n\nInputs:\n\n- `ledger_issues`;\n- `ledger_labels`;\n- `ledger_issue_relationships`;\n- `ledger_auth_issue_links` as annotations, not standalone nodes by default;\n- `ledger_session_issue_links` as history counts/annotations, not standalone nodes by default;\n- conflict/sync state as node annotations.\n\nRules:\n\n- Parent/child edges come from `parent_child` relationships, not label parsing at render time.\n- Blocks/duplicates/related/references edges come from canonical relationships.\n- Auth requests render as issue-attached shelves/annotations by default, e.g. closed issue with linked auth request evidence.\n- Dead/historical sessions render as counts/detail, not graph nodes.\n- Active/idle sessions can render as small actor glyph annotations attached to the issue if reliable current context exists.\n- Edge labels are hidden by default.\n\n### Work mode\n\nWork mode can include first-class operational nodes:\n\n- project/repo;\n- issue;\n- work unit;\n- branch;\n- session;\n- auth request;\n- commit;\n- artifact/provider nodes when relevant.\n\nRules:\n\n- Work-unit edges use canonical `ledger_issue_id` links.\n- Auth edges use `ledger_auth_issue_links`.\n- Session edges use `ledger_session_issue_links` and `sessions.parent_id`.\n- Branch/worktree data remains operational and can still come from work scanner/branches tables.\n- Work mode may show auth requests as nodes because it is an operational process view.\n\n### Activity mode\n\nActivity should become recent ledger events plus live operational state.\n\nInputs:\n\n- recent `ledger_events`;\n- pending/running auth requests;\n- active/idle sessions and channel-connected sessions;\n- recent work-unit state changes;\n- sync/conflict events.\n\nActivity nodes should prioritize recency and actionability. It is acceptable for activity mode to omit older dead sessions and old closed issues unless they are connected to recent events.\n\n### Deterministic layout rules\n\nThe backend should provide layout hints; frontend performs actual coordinates.\n\nIssue parent/child layout:\n\n- parent issue gets `layout.role='parent'` and `group_id` equal to parent issue ID;\n- children get `role='child'`, same `group_id`, and stable `order` by priority/status/updated/title;\n- parent should be left/center, children arranged in a regular column or grid to the right;\n- do not let force layout stack child issues randomly.\n\nAuth evidence layout:\n\n- auth requests in issue mode are `annotation` records anchored to an issue, not independent force nodes;\n- in work/auth mode they can be regular nodes with `anchor_id`/edge to issue/work unit.\n\nSession layout:\n\n- active/idle sessions can be `actor` annotations/glyphs anchored to issue/work unit/branch;\n- session parent/child groups use `sessions.parent_id` and can be collapsed by default;\n- dead sessions stay in issue detail history unless the user selects a history/session layer.\n\nComponent layout:\n\n- disconnected singleton issues should not dominate the layout. Sort by updated/created and place in a predictable grid after connected components.\n- connected components should remain stable across refreshes when node IDs do not change.\n\n### Node semantics\n\nIssue node detail should include enough data for the right detail pane:\n\n- canonical issue ID;\n- display alias/short ID;\n- project/repo identity;\n- status/resolution/kind/priority;\n- labels;\n- body excerpt;\n- comment count;\n- relationship counts;\n- auth evidence count/status;\n- active session count;\n- historical session count;\n- sync/conflict state.\n\nSession actor glyphs should include:\n\n- agent type (`claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, etc.);\n- status (`active`, `idle`, `stale`);\n- processing flag if available;\n- last activity;\n- anchor issue/work unit/branch.\n\n### Filters/layers\n\nFilters should move from path-ish repo names to logical project/repo identities once available. During migration, accept old repo IDs/names and canonical project IDs.\n\nLayer controls should reflect node/annotation availability:\n\n- issue;\n- relationships;\n- auth evidence;\n- work units;\n- live sessions;\n- historical sessions;\n- conflicts/sync;\n- provider/artifact where relevant.\n\nIf a layer has no data, expose it as disabled rather than silently disappearing when that would confuse the user.\n\n### Tests\n\nBackend tests:\n\n- issue graph uses ledger relationships, not git-bug labels/body parsing;\n- parent/child relationships produce stable layout hints;\n- auth requests are annotations in issue mode and nodes in work mode;\n- dead sessions are omitted from default issue graph but counted in detail metadata;\n- active/idle sessions produce actor annotations when linked;\n- graph filters accept legacy repo IDs and canonical project IDs during migration;\n- provider/artifact modes still return existing indexed graph data.\n\nFrontend/browser tests or smoke checks:\n\n- issue mode with one umbrella and children has regular geometry;\n- edge labels are hidden by default;\n- selecting an issue opens compact detail with body/comment/auth/session metadata available;\n- work mode shows work units/auth/session nodes without making issue mode noisy;\n- empty/disabled layers are understandable;\n- graph remains nonblank at desktop and mobile-ish viewport sizes.\n\n### Non-goals\n\n- Do not implement a physics/animation system for live agents here beyond stable actor overlay contracts.\n- Do not rewrite provider/artifact graph storage unless necessary.\n- Do not make graph tables canonical ledger tables.\n- Do not parse arbitrary issue prose for semantic edges in the request path.\n\n### Done check\n\nAfter this issue, the graph should be a readable projection of ledger relationships and operational links, with deterministic issue/auth/session semantics. The UI may still be iterated, but the backend contract should no longer force a graph refactor when issue routes become ledger-backed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}